{"id": "EUVD-2026-93107", "enisaUuid": "85a20892-889d-3be7-be35-3c434f1da0ce", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ndrm/amdgpu: fix rmmio iounmap skipped on device removal\n\namdgpu_pci_remove() calls drm_dev_unplug() before fini_sw(), so\ndrm_dev_enter() is already false there and the iounmap() guarded by it\nis skipped. This .remove path runs on both hot-unplug and plain rmmod,\nso the register BAR ioremap mapping leaks one instance per unload.\n\nUnmap rmmio unconditionally (guard only on non-NULL) and drop the now\nunused idx.\n\n(cherry picked from commit dd6f86a97260e5207d3329ad03aa89fdad61b1e6)", "datePublished": "2026-10-06T08:44:22", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:15:10", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e81502d6791df9ecd003bfb2ca44f0d1f1b38439", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/cd55dde2b63789a3dafe982c89844f537501d096", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a645584c3ccc493ee835f77155829442bd7578c3", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/5155002b03b24ba3ef91c5c313b8cf0171b24904"], "aliases": ["GHSA-7xg7-f7wr-mr4q", "CVE-2026-98179"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.18, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "193d5fc7-781f-379f-ba4d-79ee45f54e75", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.17"}, {"id": "199810c8-b086-3e80-a3c7-5b3c11f3d681", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.112"}, {"id": "248b41cd-ddce-3db9-a10e-fde54326b9d8", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.8"}, {"id": "69bcf436-ee67-34fa-9cf8-dc900d8ebd2d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "62d5f9f7110ad374db67ab4820f4ff2d916c3cdb <5155002b03b24ba3ef91c5c313b8cf0171b24904"}, {"id": "73d2e40f-8152-3b5e-9ac0-fb88f05f1f46", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.54"}, {"id": "9a41ef5c-eeab-3e33-af70-0e5667